+// gopher-lua/38: an integer key under MaxArrayIndex (67108864) set on an
+// empty table allocates an array of that many slots: t[2^24] = 1 takes 256 MB
+// (the reference keeps a sparse key in the hash part). Measured, like the
+// tail call pin; the program itself gives the same results on both sides.
+func TestHegelPinSparseArrayAllocation(t *testing.T) {
